      "completion_tokens": 1344,
      "output": "At its most basic level, **water** is a chemical compound with the chemical formula **$H_2O$**. This means that each molecule of water is made up of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom.\n\nHere is a breakdown of what water is, how it is structured, and why it is unique:\n\n### 1. Chemical Structure\n*   **Composition:** It consists of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom.\n*   **Polarity:** The water molecule has a bent shape (like a V). Because oxygen is more \"electronegative\" (it pulls electrons toward itself) than hydrogen, the molecule has a positive end and a negative end. This makes water a **polar molecule**.\n*   **Hydrogen Bonding:** The positive end of one water molecule is attracted to the negative end of another. These weak attractions are called hydrogen bonds. They are responsible for many of water's unique physical properties.\n\n### 2. Physical Properties\nWater is the only common substance on Earth that naturally exists as a solid, liquid, and gas at temperatures commonly found on the planet.\n*   **The Universal Solvent:** Because of its polarity, water is excellent at dissolving other substances. It can dissolve more substances than any other liquid, which is why it is essential for biological processes.\n*   **High Boiling and Melting Points:** Despite being a small molecule, water has a very high boiling point (100°C or 212°F) and a relatively high melting point (0°C or 32°F) compared to similar molecules. This is due to the strong hydrogen bonds holding the molecules together.\n*   **Density Anomaly:** Unlike most substances, water is less dense as a solid (ice) than as a liquid. This is because the hydrogen bonds in ice form a rigid, open crystal lattice that takes up more space. This is why ice floats, which insulates liquid water below it, allowing life to survive in frozen lakes.\n\n### 3. Role in Life\nWater is the foundation of life as we know it.\n*   **Biochemistry:** It is the medium in which all chemical reactions in the human body and other living organisms take place.\n*   **Habitat:** It covers about 71% of the Earth's surface and makes up about 60% of the human body.\n\nIn summary, water is a simple molecule ($H_2O$) that, due to its unique structure and bonding, acts as the essential solvent and medium for life on Earth."
